{"base_rate":0.30028735632183906,"brier":0.13570488505747128,"bss":0.3541395164221922,"bss_hi":0.44519749975540523,"bss_lo":0.26172623114053867,"chart":{"base":[451.4,138.2],"fp":[304.7,343.9],"lead":"62,272.7 272,254.2 482,216.6 692,164.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.35 — higher than 61% of cities","fp":"low end +10pp, high end +4pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 88% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 10%; promised 82% → rained 83%"},"rel":"66.3,421.5 203.6,330.5 579.6,108.5"},"country":"DZ","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.08882183908045976,"ess":361.9358314378075,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Algiers</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Algiers rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (97%), believe about\n<b>91%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>11%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 696 days, 2024-04-27 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 12.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.35, ranked 52 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(28&ndash;88) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>325</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>97%</td><td class='num'><b>91%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Algiers</b> <span class=\"muted\">DZ</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.35</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>28&ndash;88\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>696 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Algiers &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Algiers\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 71.28712328767124,352.0821917808219 101.40924999999999,309.2 177.24465753424658,222.43835616438358 295.2797183098592,100.02816901408454 400.2797297297298,18.0 400.2797297297298,47.51351351351349 295.2797183098592,176.92957746478874 177.24465753424658,297.2328767123288 101.40924999999999,359.25 71.28712328767124,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"272.6954022988506\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"272.6954022988506\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,342.8 71.28712328767124,352.0821917808219 101.40924999999999,300.1 177.24465753424658,232.4109589041096 295.2797183098592,110.28169014084506 400.2797297297298,52.43243243243245\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 11% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 325 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"342.8\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"71.28712328767124\" cy=\"352.0821917808219\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 12%&amp;#10;It rained 22% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"101.40924999999999\" cy=\"300.1\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 34%&amp;#10;It rained 41% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"177.24465753424658\" cy=\"232.4109589041096\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 67%&amp;#10;It rained 75% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"295.2797183098592\" cy=\"110.28169014084506\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 91% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"400.2797297297298\" cy=\"52.43243243243245\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(30%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Algiers the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.30) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.02).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>6%</td><td class='num'>-0.019</td><td class='num'>4.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>151</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.276</td><td class='num'>7.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>195</td><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'>0.300</td><td class='num'>10.9%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>170</td><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'>0.304</td><td class='num'>12.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":36.73225,"lon":3.08746,"n":696,"n_cities":134,"name":"Algiers","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":325,"obs":0.1076923076923077,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.03753424657534246,"n":73,"obs":0.0821917808219178,"sig":false},{"hi":0.23,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.12262499999999998,"n":80,"obs":0.225,"sig":true},{"hi":0.5,"lo":0.23,"mean":0.3368493150684932,"n":73,"obs":0.410958904109589,"sig":false},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.5,"mean":0.6702816901408453,"n":71,"obs":0.7464788732394366,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9668918918918921,"n":74,"obs":0.9054054054054054,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":12.3,"provisional":false,"rank":52,"rank_hi":88.02499999999998,"rank_lo":28.0,"reliability":0.008399696453539982,"resolution":0.08348654245695097,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"algiers","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Algiers"}